{"reference":"2 Chronicles 3","book":"2 Chronicles","chapter":3,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"historical_context","title":"Historical Context","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The temple construction described here is presented within 2 Chronicles 1–7 as the completion of David’s preparations. The larger account moves from Solomon’s wisdom and building work to the ark, glory, dedication prayer, fire, celebration, divine promise, and warning.","verse_refs":["2 Chronicles 3:1-17"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_2_chronicles_003_a0995d872c4337c9146a3a99"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"fact"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}